Privacy Policy for SOS Family Connect

Last updated: June 16, 2026

SOS Family Connect ("we", "our", or "the App") respects your privacy and is committed to protecting your personal information. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect information when you use our application.

1. Information We Collect

When you use SOS Family Connect, we may collect the following information:

• Location Information:
We collect your location information only when you allow permission. Location data is used to provide emergency location sharing and safety features with your trusted contacts.

• Account Information:
If you create an account, we may collect information such as your email address, username, or account identifiers to provide authentication and app functionality.

• Device Information:
We may collect basic device information necessary for app performance, security, and troubleshooting.

2. How We Use Your Information

We use collected information to:

• Provide SOS emergency alert services
• Share your location with contacts you choose
• Maintain and improve app functionality
• Provide account and customer support
• Ensure app security and reliability

3. Location Data Usage

SOS Family Connect uses location services to help users share their current location during emergency situations.

Your location:
• Is only collected with your permission
• Is used only for safety and emergency features
• Is not sold or used for advertising purposes

You can disable location access at any time from your device settings.

4. Data Sharing

We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information.

Your information may only be shared:
• With contacts you choose for SOS emergency purposes
• When required by law
• To protect the safety and security of our users

5. Data Security

We take reasonable measures to protect your information from unauthorized access, loss, misuse, or disclosure.

However, no method of electronic storage or transmission is completely secure.

6. Children's Privacy

SOS Family Connect is designed to help families and users stay safe. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children without appropriate consent.

7. Third-Party Services

The App may use third-party services that help us provide functionality, such as authentication, database services, analytics, or notifications. These services may process information according to their own privacy policies.

8. Your Rights

You may request access, correction, or deletion of your personal information by contacting us.

9. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated date.

